# Session credentials. Everything here is minted locally by `make certs` and
# ignored, with one deliberate exception: demo-ca.crt is the public CA of the
# demo server, committed so a downloaded client can verify it without being
# handed a file out of band.
#
# It is a separate path from ca.crt rather than the same file because the two
# have opposite lifetimes. ca.crt is scratch - generate_certs.sh owns it, and
# reissues it whenever this machine needs to serve - while demo-ca.crt is a
# promise to every client already in the wild and must never be rewritten. When
# they shared a path, `make certs` and `make play` replaced the promise with
# scratch, and no client could reach the demo server again.
#
# The pattern is `certs/*` and not `certs/`: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a `!certs/demo-ca.crt` under `certs/` would never be
# reached and the negation would silently do nothing.
certs/*
!certs/demo-ca.crt

